[?2004l[?2004h> INCREMENTAL BACKUP FIX - May 6, 2026
[?2004l[?2004h> =====================================
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> PROBLEM:
[?2004l[?2004h> Incremental backups were producing corrupt/incomplete archives due to a race condition.
[?2004l[?2004h> The script was updating the timestamp reference BEFORE tar finished writing the archive.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ROOT CAUSE:
[?2004l[?2004h> In incremental.sh, the tar command was backgrounded with '&', then the timestamp was
[?2004l[?2004h> immediately updated with 'date +%s > $TIMESTAMP_FILE', and only AFTER that did the
[?2004l[?2004h> script wait for tar to complete with 'wait $TAR_PID'.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This caused the reference time to be updated before tar finished reading all files,
[?2004l[?2004h> leading to:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Missed files in subsequent backups
[?2004l[?2004h> - Inconsistent state tracking
[?2004l[?2004h> - Archives that appeared complete but were missing data
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> SOLUTION:
[?2004l[?2004h> Swapped the order of operations in the incremental branch:
[?2004l[?2004h>   OLD ORDER:
[?2004l[?2004h>     1. Start tar in background
[?2004l[?2004h>     2. Update timestamp  <-- WRONG: happens before tar finishes
[?2004l[?2004h>     3. Wait for tar
[?2004l[?2004h>   
[?2004l[?2004h>   NEW ORDER:
[?2004l[?2004h>     1. Start tar in background
[?2004l[?2004h>     2. Wait for tar       <-- CORRECT: wait first
[?2004l[?2004h>     3. Update timestamp  <-- Only update after tar completes
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> VERIFICATION:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Fixed script now produces small incremental archives containing only changed files
[?2004l[?2004h> - Archives extract successfully without corruption
[?2004l[?2004h> - Multiple sequential incrementals work correctly
